          "ruleId": "answer-checks-undeclared",
          "ruleIndex": 16,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Asset ARB on arbitrum is read through latestRoundData, but its configuration has no answerChecks, so it does not say whether the protocol checks the time of the answer, that the answer is above 0, or that the round is complete. This is a best practice of this tool, not a rule in the Chainlink pages on Data Feeds or on ethereum.org. Fix: List in answerChecks what the protocol checks on every read: updatedAt, answerPositive and, where it applies, roundComplete."
